-- ============================================================
-- MIGRATION_cie10_seed.sql
-- Seed for cie10_codes (created in MIGRATION_nom024_program.sql)
--
-- CIE-10 (ICD-10 Spanish) diagnosis catalog for a Mexican
-- primary-care consultorio. Full catalog: 12430 codes
-- (12425 from source + 5 WHO emergency U-codes).
--
-- SOURCE: SQLite catalog `DBCIE.db` from the open-source Android app
--   "CIE10_v2" (github.com/josemsb/cie10, app/src/main/assets/DBCIE.db),
--   which bundles the official CIE-10 catalog in Spanish (descriptions
--   match the Mexican CEMECE/DGE CIE-10 wording, e.g. E11.9
--   "DIABETES MELLITUS NO INSULINODEPENDIENTE SIN MENCION DE
--   COMPLICACION"). Spot-verified against known official entries
--   (A00.0, J06.9, I10, K21.0, N39.0, M54.5, Z00.0, R51...).
--
-- NOTES:
-- * Codes keep the official dot format: 4-char codes as A00.0,
--   3-char categories as-is (I10, R51).
-- * WHO dual-classification codes keep their official marker:
--   dagger (etiology, e.g. A06.5†) and asterisk (manifestation,
--   e.g. H62.0*; 3-char categories like G01* keep the bare marker).
--   65 dagger + 294 asterisk codes.
-- * `chapter` is the official CIE-10 chapter letter block
--   (e.g. 'A00-B99' = Capítulo I). Chapter XXII (U00-U99) rows are
--   the WHO 2020+ emergency codes for COVID-19, added manually since
--   the source catalog predates them.
-- * Descriptions are kept verbatim from the source (uppercase
--   Spanish). Idempotent: re-runs skip existing codes.
-- * To expand/refresh: replace with the full CEMECE CIE-10 catalog
--   (Catalogo de Enfermedades, datos.gob.mx / DGE) using the same
--   insert ... on conflict (code) do nothing pattern.
-- ============================================================

